---
description: Filter types, sources, presets, hierarchy, and SQL template syntax
globs: dashboards/**/*.yaml
alwaysApply: false
---

<rule>
<meta>
  This rule covers filter definitions for A7S Skipper dashboards: 8 filter types, 6 source types, hierarchy/cascade, URL serialization, and filter pools.
  Activate when writing `filters:` blocks at dashboard, tab, section, or widget level.
</meta>

<concepts>
  <hierarchy>Root filters → Dashboard filters → Tab filters → Section filters → Widget `inline_filters`</hierarchy>
  <cascade>Widgets inherit all ancestor filters. Control scope with `filters: { include: [...] }` or `filters: { exclude: [...] }`.</cascade>
  <rbac_note>Filters shape data inside an already accessible dashboard. They do not grant access.</rbac_note>
</concepts>

<schema>
  <filter_definition>
    ```yaml
    filters:
      - id: date_range                     # Required. Unique identifier
        type: date_range                   # Required. See filter types below
        column: install_date               # Required (nullable). Target column in SQL
        label: Date Range                  # Optional (inferred from id at runtime)
        placeholder: Select...             # Optional. Empty state text
        icon: Calendar                     # Optional. Lucide icon name
        required: true                     # Optional. Must have a value
        clearable: true                    # Optional. Allow clearing (default: true)
        searchable: true                   # Optional. Enable search in select
        ui_only: false                     # Optional. No SQL effect
        serializable: true                 # Optional. Serialize to URL
        pool: geo                          # Optional. Progressive disclosure pool
        source: {}                         # Optional. How to get options
        selection: {}                      # Optional. Selection behavior
        default: {}                        # Optional. Default value
        presets: []                        # Optional. Predefined presets
        # Boolean only:
        true_label: "Yes"                  # Optional (default: "Yes")
        false_label: "No"                  # Optional (default: "No")
        true_value: 1                      # Optional (default: 1)
        false_value: 0                     # Optional (default: 0)
        # Segmented only:
        allow_none: false                  # Optional. Allow deselecting all
        icon_only: false                   # Optional. Icons only, labels as tooltips
        # Slider only:
        slider_config: {}                  # Required for slider type
    ```
  </filter_definition>
</schema>

<options>
  <filter_types>
    | Type | UI Component | Value Type | Notes |
    |---|---|---|---|
    | `select` | MultiSelect dropdown | `string[]` or `string` | Requires `source` |
    | `date_range` | DateRangePicker | `{ start, end, preset? }` | — |
    | `relative_date` | Select dropdown | `{ preset }` | Preset-based |
    | `number_range` | Min/max inputs | `{ min?, max? }` | — |
    | `search` | Text input | `string` | — |
    | `boolean` | Toggle (Yes/No) | `boolean` | Requires `default` |
    | `segmented` | Toggle group | `string \| string[]` | — |
    | `slider` | Range slider | `{ min?, max? }` or `number` | Requires `slider_config` |
  </filter_types>

  <source_types>
    | Source | Key Fields | Description |
    |---|---|---|
    | `static` | `type: static`, `options: [{ value, label, icon?, disabled? }]` | Hardcoded list |
    | `query` | `type: query`, `sql`, `value_field?`, `label_field?` | ClickHouse SQL |
    | `projection` | `type: projection`, `projection`, `value_field`, `label_field?`, `order_by?`, `limit?` | From DuckDB projection |
    | `cascade` | `type: cascade`, `depends_on: <filter_id>` | Depends on parent filter |
    | `remote` | `type: remote`, `search_endpoint`, `min_search_length?` | Server-side search |
    | SQL shorthand | `sql`, `value_field?`, `label_field?` (no `type`) | Expanded at load time |
  </source_types>

  <selection_config>
    ```yaml
    selection:
      empty_means: all           # all | none
      allow_select_all: true     # Show "Select all" button
      allow_exclude_mode: true   # Allow switching to exclude mode
      min_selected: 1            # Min items required
      max_selected: 5            # Max items allowed (1 = single-select mode)
    ```
  </selection_config>

  <slider_config>
    ```yaml
    slider_config:
      min: 0                     # Required. Lower bound
      max: 100                   # Required. Upper bound (must be > min)
      step: 1                    # Optional. Step size (default: 1)
      range: true                # Optional. true = two thumbs (default), false = single
      show_input: true           # Optional. Numeric inputs alongside slider
      format: "{value} yrs"      # Optional. Display format
    ```
  </slider_config>

  <url_serialization>
    | Value type | URL format | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | String | raw | `f_status=active` |
    | Array (include) | comma-separated | `f_channel=fb,google` |
    | Array (exclude) | `!` prefix | `f_channel=!fb,google` |
    | Date range (custom) | `start~end` | `f_date_range=2024-01-01~2024-02-01` |
    | Date range (preset) | `preset:<id>` | `f_date_range=preset:last_30_days` |
    | Boolean | `true`/`false` | `f_active=true` |
    | Number range / Slider | `min~max` | `f_age=18~65` |

    | Scope | Default serializable | Behavior |
    |---|---|---|
    | Dashboard filters | `true` | Auto-synced to URL |
    | Section filters | `false` | Share link only if `serializable: true` |
    | Widget inline filters | `false` | Share link only if `serializable: true` |
  </url_serialization>
</options>

<examples>
  <boolean_filter>
    ```yaml
    - id: is_organic
      type: boolean
      column: is_organic
      label: Organic
      default: false

    # Custom labels and SQL values
    - id: status
      type: boolean
      column: status
      label: Status
      true_label: Active
      false_label: Inactive
      true_value: "'active'"
      false_value: "'inactive'"
      default: true
    ```
    SQL: `column = 1` / `column = 0` (default), or `column = <true_value>` / `column = <false_value>`.
  </boolean_filter>

  <segmented_filter>
    ```yaml
    # Single-select with icons (clearable by default)
    - id: platform
      type: segmented
      column: platform
      default: ios
      source:
        type: static
        options:
          - { value: ios, label: iOS, icon: Apple }
          - { value: android, label: Android, icon: Smartphone }

    # SQL-loaded options
    - id: country
      type: segmented
      column: country
      source:
        sql: "SELECT DISTINCT country FROM {{source:main}} ORDER BY country LIMIT 8"

    # Icon-only UI toggle
    - id: view_mode
      type: segmented
      column: null
      ui_only: true
      default: table
      icon_only: true
      source:
        type: static
        options:
          - { value: table, label: Table view, icon: Table }
          - { value: chart, label: Chart view, icon: BarChart }
    ```
  </segmented_filter>

  <slider_filter>
    ```yaml
    # Dual-thumb range
    - id: age_range
      type: slider
      column: user_age
      label: Age Range
      slider_config: { min: 0, max: 100, step: 1, range: true, show_input: true, format: "{value} yrs" }
      default: { min: 18, max: 65 }

    # Single-thumb minimum threshold
    - id: min_spend
      type: slider
      column: total_spend
      label: Minimum Spend
      slider_config: { min: 0, max: 10000, step: 100, range: false, format: "${value}" }
      default: 500
    ```
  </slider_filter>

  <single_select>
    When `selection.max_selected: 1`, select switches to single-select mode:
    auto-applies on click, no checkboxes, popover closes on selection, clearable.

    ```yaml
    - id: currency
      type: select
      column: currency
      label: Currency
      source:
        type: static
        options:
          - { value: USD, label: "US Dollar" }
          - { value: EUR, label: Euro }
      selection: { max_selected: 1 }
      default: USD
    ```
  </single_select>

  <date_range_with_presets>
    ```yaml
    - id: date_range
      type: date_range
      column: install_date
      presets:
        - { id: today, label: Today, tag: Live }
        - { id: yesterday, label: Yesterday, tag: Live }
        - { id: last_7_days, label: "Last 7 days", tag: Rolling }
        - { id: last_14_days, label: "Last 14 days", tag: Rolling }
        - { id: last_30_days, label: "Last 30 days", tag: Rolling }
        - { id: this_month, label: "This month" }
        - { id: last_month, label: "Last month" }
      default:
        preset: last_14_days
    ```
  </date_range_with_presets>

  <widget_filter_scope>
    ```yaml
    widgets:
      - id: my_widget
        type: rich_table
        filters:
          include: [date_range]       # Only these from parent scopes
        # OR
        filters:
          exclude: [media_source]     # All except these
        inline_filters:               # Widget-scoped
          - id: local_filter
            type: select
            column: status
            source:
              type: static
              options:
                - { value: active, label: Active }
                - { value: paused, label: Paused }
    ```
  </widget_filter_scope>
</examples>

<patterns>
  <filter_pools>
    Filters with `pool` are hidden by default, shown via "+ Add filter" button.

    ```yaml
    filters:
      - id: date_range
        type: date_range
        column: dt
        default: { preset: last_14_days }

      # Hidden by default — pool: language
      - id: native_language
        type: select
        column: native_language
        pool: language
        source:
          type: query
          sql: "SELECT DISTINCT native_language AS value FROM {{source:main}}"
    ```

    Pool labels auto-derived: `snake_case` → Title Case (e.g. `campaign_details` → "Campaign Details").
    User customization persists in localStorage.
  </filter_pools>

  <filter_groups>
    Optional field in `+layout.yaml` (folder layout) that groups tabs and binds each group to specific filters.
    Controls UI visibility and navigation only — does NOT affect SQL rendering or URL serialization.

    Two modes:
    - **Classic** (no `filter_groups`): all tabs shown inline, all filters visible.
    - **Grouped**: tabs split by group; only the active group's filters are shown in the filter panel.

    ```yaml
    filter_groups:
      - id: content              # Required. Unique group identifier
        tabs: [overview, detail] # Required. Tab IDs belonging to this group
        filters: [date_range, platform]  # Required. Filter IDs visible when group is active
        label: Content           # Optional. Display label for collapsed group dropdown
        color: blue              # Optional. Accent color (blue|violet|amber|emerald|rose|cyan|teal|indigo)
        collapse: false          # Optional. true (default) | false | { threshold: N }
    ```

    Collapse behavior:
    - `true` (default) — group tabs render as a single dropdown selector.
    - `false` — group tabs render inline in the tab bar.
    - `{ threshold: N }` — inline when tab count ≤ N, otherwise collapse to dropdown.

    Interaction with filter pools:
    - Pool visibility is scoped within the group-filtered set. When a group is active, the "+ Add filter" menu shows only pool filters whose IDs appear in that group's `filters` list.
    - Filters not listed in any group are hidden while any group is active.
  </filter_groups>

  <shared_filters>
    Root-level `_shared/_filters.yaml` inherited by all dashboards:
    ```yaml
    - id: date_range
      type: date_range
      column: install_date
      default: { preset: last_14_days }
    ```

    Override rule: if dashboard defines ANY filters, root filters are completely replaced.

    Tab-level override in composite tabs: `<tab>/_shared/_filters.yaml` replaces dashboard filters for that tab.
    Priority: tab `_shared/_filters.yaml` > section `filters:` > dashboard `_shared/_filters.yaml`.
  </shared_filters>

  <smart_search>
    Smart search is a rich_table feature, NOT a filter type. Configured via `filtering.global_search`:

    ```yaml
    filtering:
      global_search:
        enabled: true
        show_token_pills: false
        token_pills_expanded: true
    ```

    Search results participate in cross-filtering: narrowing select options, locking search-derived columns (blue ring), auto-pruning invalid selections.
  </smart_search>

  <inline_column_filters>
    Column-level filters use bi-directional cross-filtering: each select dropdown shows only values existing given all other active inline filters.

    - Independent — changing one does not reset others
    - Pruning — if a selected value disappears, it's auto-removed
    - Works with all datasource types
    - Data presets change base SQL, so options reflect the active subset
  </inline_column_filters>

  <section_navigation>
    Sections and widgets have DOM `id` attributes (`id="s-{sectionId}"`, `id="w-{widgetId}"`):
    ```text
    /dashboards/<root>/<dashboard>/<tab>#s:section_id
    /dashboards/<root>/<dashboard>/<tab>#w:widget_id
    ```
    Collapsed sections auto-expand when navigated to.
    `shareable: true` shows a share button generating a link with filter context + anchor.
  </section_navigation>
</patterns>

<rules>
  <validation_constraints>
    - `select` filters REQUIRE a `source`
    - `boolean` filters REQUIRE `default`
    - `slider` filters REQUIRE `slider_config` with `min < max`
    - Filters with `pool` CANNOT have `default` (hidden filter with default = silent data filtering)
    - `clearable` applies to: select (single-select), segmented (single-select)
  </validation_constraints>

  <sql_rendering>
    - Single value → `column = 'value'`
    - Multi-select → `column IN ('a', 'b')`
    - Empty/cleared → `1=1` (no filter)
    - Boolean → `column = 1` or `column = 0` (or custom values)
    - Segmented no selection → `1=1`
    - Slider range → `column >= min AND column <= max`
    - Slider single → `column >= value`
    - `.required` / `.or_false` — when filter is empty, render `1=0` (zero rows) to gate heavy queries until the user picks a value.
  </sql_rendering>
</rules>

